                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_13\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit's message explicitly cites \"fixed generated table factory method argument ordering\". The corresponding hunk in fix_commit_diff.txt (TableFactoryRenderer.java) changes:\n\n    line(\"return \", Table, \".of(t, name, namespace, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\");\nto\n    line(\"return \", Table, \".of(t, namespace, name, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\");\n\ni.e. swapping the (name, namespace) argument order to the correct (namespace, name) order in the generated `get<Table>(Transaction t, String name, ...)` factory method for generic tables.\n\nSearching the candidates for this exact code, candidate_13.diff is the commit that first introduces the `namespace` parameter into this generated factory call. Before this commit, the generated code was:\n\n    _(\"return \", Table, \".of(t, name, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\");\n\nCandidate_13 changes it to:\n\n    _(\"return \", Table, \".of(t, name, namespace, Triggers.getAllTriggers(t, sharedTriggers, triggers));\");\n\nThis is the exact buggy ordering (name, namespace) that the fix commit later corrects to (namespace, name). This makes sense: candidate_13 introduced namespace-awareness to the generated TableFactory (adding a `namespace` field/constructor param to TableFactoryRenderer), and in doing so placed `name` before `namespace` in the `Table.of(...)` factory call \u2014 inconsistent with the actual static factory signature `of(Transaction t, Namespace namespace, String name, ...)` used elsewhere, causing a namespace/name mismatch bug in generated code.\n\nCandidate_16 later only changes the rendering helper method from `_(...)` to `line(...)` (a refactor of the renderer's internal API) but keeps the same buggy argument order, confirming the bug was inherited rather than introduced there. Candidate_23 is essentially the fix commit itself, correcting the order back to (namespace, name).\n\nTherefore candidate_13 is the commit that introduced the bug.\n"
